 "title": "Contamination signs: plaster, wax, ester consolidant, burnt",
 "description": "On the standard-resolution stream (high-res transferred first); each sign only when it passes its own B6b gate (check.acquisition, per sign; else that sign is 'gated: noise in <window>'). Kernel: -1e5 x SG17 quadratic 2nd derivative of log10(1/max(R,1e-3)). sharp(c, h, f0, f1) = mean N[c-h..c+h] - 0.5 x (mean N[c-f1..c-f0] + mean N[c+f0..c+f1]). Plaster: joint load = min over the two gypsum bands of (sharp - fauna median) / plaster contrast, fires above the cut. Wax: both sharp tests. Ester: one sharp test. Burnt: the heat check (check.heat). Signs add a FLAG (badge + text) and block an evidence lift (plaster, wax, ester; burnt does not block); they never change the verdict (DECISIONS 53). No clay sign (DECISIONS 41). Soft tier ('possible thin coating', a note only): when no hard contaminant sign fired (plaster, wax, ester, C1) and the scan is eligible (standard-resolution class always; other classes only when N2(2000-2100) <= the eligibility cut), the note fires if any CHECKED sign's statistic reaches its soft line (ester sharp, plaster joint load here; C1 excess in check.c1). It changes no verdict, blocks no lift and is not a flag.",
 "licence": "CC-BY-4.0",
 "created": "2026-10-03",
 "provenance": {
  "basis": "Plaster screen v3 and heat screen v1 frozen on an unreleased archaeological fauna series (statistics only, no site named); wax and ester tests from the SPYDER Bone warnings study (07). Clean pool false alarms: plaster 1, wax 0, ester 0 of 1,201 scans.",
  "soft_tier": "Phase 0c (DECISIONS 74, 76), design A at a 2% clean false-alarm budget: one common quantile of the in-pool clean statistics (C1 excess, ester, plaster load) so the union false-alarm rate in the pool is 2%: C1 6.6 (C1 truncated 6.1, the same offset below its cut), ester 13.1, plaster 0.026. Independent clean sets: about 1.4% pooled; coats at the applied thickness (standard-resolution): PVA 80%, acrylic 95%, cellulose nitrate 36%; protein glue 3-8% (no shippable tier). High-resolution scans noisier than N2(2000-2100) 60 are not eligible (ester noise gives 7.5-25% false alarms)."
 },
